    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347">

                <pb facs="0552" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2680</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-10T21:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 10, 1916, 9 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 11, 2 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3873. Presented note in your 2983<anchor n="1" xml:id="d347-f1"/> to Von Jagow, 1 [o’clock] to-day. Had a general
                    talk with him but learned nothing particular. From general information think
                    Germany will not answer this note. Von
                        Jagow said German note had not made any express condition. It is
                    possible Bernstorff may be authorized
                    to declare against propaganda in America, plots, etc. Talk here of Sweden coming
                    in. No foundation apparent except that large Swedish military commission is here
                    and made much of.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
